SCOPE CONTROL

allow script to define the scope within a block of code:

table = { scope variables here }
scope table {
	
}

and

scope { scope variables here } {
	
}

or 

table = { scope variables here }
table {
	
}

and

{ scope variables here } {
	
}

or have either of these and

with table {
	
}

(which would extend the scope vs isolate it)

This would allow describe to basically create a snapshot of a function
(at any point in a table or array too) and save it as a string, this string
can then simply just be imported